---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import AffiliateLink from "../../components/AffiliateLink.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Best Co-Op Games on Switch (2026)"
  description="The best local and online co-op games on Nintendo Switch in 2026, from Mario Kart to Animal Crossing — and where to buy them cheapest."
>
  <article class="post">
    <h1>Best Co-Op Games on Switch (2026)</h1>
    <p class="meta">Roundup · Updated 2026-08-05</p>

    <p>
      The Switch is the best couch-co-op console on the market. If you play with
      family or friends in the same room, these are the titles worth owning.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Mario Kart 8 Deluxe</h2>
    <p>
      The gold standard for pick-up-and-play multiplayer. Up to 4 systems locally,
      12 online, and smart-steering makes it kid-friendly.
    </p>
    <AffiliateLink network="amazon" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Mario+Kart+8+Deluxe+Switch" cta="Check Mario Kart" />

    <h2>2. Super Mario Bros. Wonder</h2>
    <p>
      Up to 4 players in the same world, with the chaotic Elephant form a hit with
      younger players. The most modern 2D Mario.
    </p>
    <AffiliateLink network="amazon" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Super+Mario+Bros+Wonder+Switch" cta="Check SMB Wonder" />

    <h2>3. Animal Crossing: New Horizons</h2>
    <p>
      Not competitive — just a shared island you visit together. Perfect for relaxed
      co-op sessions.
    </p>
    <AffiliateLink network="amazon" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Animal+Crossing+New+Horizons+Switch" cta="Check Animal Crossing" />

    <h2>4. Pokémon Scarlet & Violet</h2>
    <p>
      Four-player co-op in the open world — explore, battle, and trade together.
    </p>
    <AffiliateLink network="amazon" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Pokemon+Scarlet+Violet+Switch" cta="Check Pokémon" />

    <h2>Buying tip</h2>
    <p>
      First-party Switch games hold price, so the "cheapest" angle is usually about
      <em>where you have credit</em> (eShop funds, retailer gift cards) rather than
      deep discounts. Watch Black Friday and the Nintendo eShop seasonal sales.
    </p>

    <p class="note">
      Prices change frequently — always verify on the store before purchasing.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .post { padding: 1.5rem 0; max-width: 720px; }
  .post h1 { font-size: 1.8rem; }
  .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .post :global(.aff-link) { margin: 0.5rem 0 1.25rem; }
  .note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
</style>
